ef 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268853 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dy\\,dx=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268853 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "07938b36-7b86-5365-9a53-980eadb141d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268853 #edb/ref 1074 "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x[\\,y\\,]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,dx & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-2) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321192 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{11}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321192 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321192 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04d2a009-9a40-5d25-99e2-4f97af963231" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321242 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321242 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321242 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b726bfa-ba4c-5d91-9f6d-6a3764d8755d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321322 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321322 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321322 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "15